---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TeamBuilder from '../components/TeamBuilder';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pokémon Team Analyzer & Team Score | Super Pokémon Team Builder" description="Analyze a six-Pokémon team with an explainable score, defensive weakness matrix, offensive type coverage, team synergy, and recommended teammates."><SiteHeader/><main id="main"><p class="eyebrow">COMPLETE TEAM REVIEW</p><h1>Pokémon Team Analyzer</h1><p class="intro">Build a team, find shared weaknesses, review type coverage and see recommended teammates. The 0–100 score is a planning heuristic, not a predicted win rate.</p><TeamBuilder focus="analyzer" client:load/><section class="seo-content"><h2>How this Pokémon team analyzer works</h2><p>The overall score combines offense (25%), defense (30%), coverage (25%) and synergy (20%). Type matchups and base stats power the analysis; abilities, moves, items, weather, Tera types and actual battle outcomes are not modeled.</p><h3>Explore the focused tools</h3><p><a href="/weakness-calculator">Check defensive weaknesses →</a></p><p><a href="/type-coverage">Calculate attacking type coverage →</a></p><h3>Frequently asked questions</h3><details><summary>Is a higher score a guaranteed stronger competitive team?</summary><p>No. Scores are uncalibrated planning heuristics for casual team building. Format legality and actual battle results depend on details this tool does not simulate.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use a partially completed team?</summary><p>Yes. Scores update as you add members, but should be considered provisional until your team is complete.</p></details></section></main><SiteFooter/></BaseLayout>
